From 89f17b5b534f3a019c78c37824c8b9bc1ca85539 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuda Adi Pratama <yudaadipratama@Yudas-MacBook-Air.local>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 05:10:51 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(integrations): add DMS/TSP integration card + config
 form (Package F, Task 5)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds the "Integrations" nav page (gated on integration.manage), a
DMS/TSP status card, and its config form backing the Task 1-4
/admin/integrations/dms admin API:

- Card status is deliberately conservative: it never claims
  "Connected" from config fields alone (GET never probes the remote
  system), only "Not connected" / "Enabled, not yet verified" /
  "Status unavailable".
- The credential field is never populated from the API (write-only,
  not returned by GET). It renders as a masked "••••••••" display
  with a Replace action; the PUT body only ever includes `credential`
  when the operator is in Replace mode AND typed a non-empty value
  (trimmed before it's sent), guarding against ever sending
  `credential: ''` (which the backend treats as "wipe the stored
  secret", vs. omitting the key which preserves it).
- extra_header_value is flagged inline as NOT secret storage, since
  (unlike credential) GET returns it in plain text.
- Test connection surfaces every backend status (reachable, auth_failed,
  timeout, unexpected_status, not_configured) with distinct plain-language
  titles. unexpected_status's copy explicitly avoids implying a bad
  credential, since it also covers a 404 from a correctly configured
  server; not_configured is kept separate from it because nothing was
  sent at all, so pointing at the base URL would be misdirection.
- No Retries control is rendered: `retries` is stored and round-tripped
  but read by nothing in Phase 1, and an inert settings control is the
  same class of failure as a shell mistaken for a working integration.
- Timeout carries max=30 and a range caption, mirroring the backend's
  Field(gt=0, le=30).
- ProtonCustomer360Page.vue gains an optional DMS/TSP section: a
  status: "unreachable" block renders an explicit "Not connected"
  notice, and mock: true renders a plainly-labeled "Mock data" banner
  independent of MockDmsClient's own "(Demo data)" field markers.
- auth_type is normalised to a real <select> option on load/after save,
  since the backend's never-configured state returns auth_type: '' —
  left unnormalised, a first-time save without opening the dropdown
  would silently send an auth scheme the operator never chose, later
  misread as a bad credential when the probe failed.
- ProtonIntegrationsPage.vue's status GET failure now also raises a
  useAlert toast, matching the config page's own load() failure
  behavior.
